From ec2c6a52369b886e9aa0a0b32a0ba1b447be1d6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filyus <filyus@filyus.ru>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:14:12 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add tokenHelper, a program that prints a registry token

`//<registry>/:tokenHelper=<absolute path>` names a program that prints the
credential for a registry, the setting of the same name that pnpm has. A raw
token is sent as `Bearer <token>`; output that starts with an auth scheme and
a space is used as the header value. The credential is supplied through the
`getAuthorization` option of npm-registry-fetch, so it is sent as a stored
`_authToken` is: same proxy and certificate settings, same http: behaviour,
same redirects.

The runner (lib/utils/token-helper.js, on @npmcli/promise-spawn) takes one
absolute path with no arguments and refuses anything else with a message that
says what to do: a two-line script for arguments, an absolute path for a bare
name, a .cmd wrapper for a .ps1 or .js file on Windows. A .cmd or .bat file
runs through cmd.exe, and a path with `"`, `%` or `!` is refused, as is one in a directory longer than 258 characters. The helper starts
in its own directory with stdin closed, has 60 seconds (SIGTERM, SIGKILL 2
seconds later, the process tree on Windows) and 1 MiB per stream, is read for 250 ms after it exits, and runs
once per registry and helper per process; a failure is cached too. Its
environment lacks the npm_config_* variables and the script directories npm
put in front of PATH, and gets NODE_OPTIONS, EDITOR, NODE_ENV and COLOR as the
user's environment had them when npm started; NPM_TOKEN_HELPER is set so that
an npm the helper runs starts no helper. Output is trimmed, a byte order mark
removed, and anything that is not a header value refused without quoting it.
stderr is shown with the exact token replaced by `***`: as warnings when the
helper fails, at verbose when it works. A failure is an ETOKENHELPER error
that carries helperExitCode and signal itself, so npm exits as for any of its errors.

Only the user and global config files may set it, and only when project config
sets none of userconfig, globalconfig and prefix (keys compared after ${VAR}
expansion). In project config, publishConfig, the environment and on the
command line it is ignored with a warning. A child npm is told which files its
parent did not trust in npm_config_token_helper_untrusted, set only when one
of them has a helper. The unscoped, slash-less and per-package-scope forms are
ignored with a warning that names the line to write instead.

The helper wins over a stored credential for the same registry, with one
warning per registry that names what is ignored; an OIDC trusted-publishing
token wins over both. publish, whoami and get-identity count a helper as a
login; logout says the setting has to be removed and names a stored token;
login and profile enable-2fa refuse; config set refuses the unscoped form and
project config.

Needs an npm-registry-fetch that provides opts.getAuthorization; the version
bundled in node_modules does not, so nothing runs a helper until that is
updated.
